<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number gold">3</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Safety, Bias, and Health Equity</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="warning-box">
          <div class="warning-stat">18%</div>
          <div class="warning-label">of published studies report formal assessment of algorithmic bias</div>
          <div class="warning-desc">Only 18% of studies assess bias across demographic groups — age, sex, ethnicity, and socioeconomic status.</div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#fef2f2;border:2px solid #fecaca;border-radius:8px;padding:30px;margin-top:20px;">
          <div style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:48px;font-weight:900;color:#dc2626;">5–12 pp</div>
          <div style="font-size:22px;color:#991b1b;margin-top:8px;line-height:1.5;">Performance disparities in sensitivity documented for underrepresented populations, particularly in dermatology AI trained on lighter skin tones.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="body-text">
        <p>Despite encouraging accuracy figures, <strong>safety and equity concerns persist</strong>. Algorithmic bias remains critically under-assessed in the published literature, creating an evidence gap that undermines confidence in AI generalizability.</p>
        <p>Adverse safety events attributable to AI recommendations were reported in <strong>fewer than 1% of prospective trials</strong>, but significant under-reporting is suspected due to the absence of standardised safety-reporting frameworks for AI-CDSS.</p>
        <p>The lack of mandatory bias auditing and safety registries — analogous to pharmacovigilance systems — represents a <strong>critical gap in the AI governance infrastructure</strong> needed for safe clinical deployment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ SECTION 4: IMPLEMENTATION GAP ═══════════ -->
<div class="anchor-section">
  <div class="anchor-label">The Translational Implementation Gap</div>
  <div class="anchor-value">&lt;5%</div>
  <div class="anchor-desc">of AI models published in peer-reviewed literature have undergone prospective clinical validation in real-world settings</div>
  <div class="anchor-sub">Despite 692 FDA-cleared AI/ML medical devices, fewer than 1 in 20 published AI models ever reach prospective validation — the critical step between research promise and clinical reality.</div>
</div>

<section class="section" style="margin-top:0;">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number red">4</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Key Barriers to Implementation</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
