      <div class="barrier-item">
        <div class="barrier-num">Barrier 1</div>
        <div class="barrier-title">Data Infrastructure</div>
        <div class="barrier-desc">Fragmented electronic health record systems and lack of interoperability standards prevent scalable AI deployment.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="barrier-item">
        <div class="barrier-num">Barrier 2</div>
        <div class="barrier-title">Regulatory Uncertainty</div>
        <div class="barrier-desc">Evolving frameworks lag behind the pace of AI development, creating ambiguity for developers and adopters.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="barrier-item">
        <div class="barrier-num">Barrier 3</div>
        <div class="barrier-title">Clinician Trust</div>
        <div class="barrier-desc">Insufficient explainability and transparency of model outputs undermine clinician confidence.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="barrier-item">
        <div class="barrier-num">Barrier 4</div>
        <div class="barrier-title">Economic Evidence</div>
        <div class="barrier-desc">Limited cost-effectiveness analyses to justify health-system investment in AI tools.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="barrier-item">
        <div class="barrier-num">Barrier 5</div>
        <div class="barrier-title">Workflow Integration</div>
        <div class="barrier-desc">Poor alignment of AI tools with existing clinical workflows impedes routine adoption.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ SECTION 5: RECOMMENDATIONS ═══════════ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-number navy">5</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Recommendations &amp; Future Directions</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <div class="recs-list">
      <div class="rec-item">
        <div class="rec-num">1</div>
        <div class="rec-text"><strong>Mandate prospective validation</strong> before clinical deployment, including multi-site and diverse-population trials to ensure real-world generalizability.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rec-item">
        <div class="rec-num">2</div>
        <div class="rec-text"><strong>Standardise bias auditing</strong> using demographic-stratified performance reporting as a publication requirement for AI diagnostic studies.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rec-item">
        <div class="rec-num">3</div>
        <div class="rec-text"><strong>Develop shared safety-reporting registries</strong> analogous to pharmacovigilance systems to track AI-CDSS adverse events systematically.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rec-item">
        <div class="rec-num">4</div>
        <div class="rec-text"><strong>Invest in interoperability</strong> through adoption of open data standards (e.g., FHIR, OMOP) to enable scalable AI integration across health systems.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rec-item">
        <div class="rec-num">5</div>
        <div class="rec-text"><strong>Prioritise explainability research</strong> to build clinician and patient trust in AI-augmented care through transparent, interpretable model outputs.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ FOOTER ═══════════ -->
<footer class="footer">
  <p>Data sources: Systematic review of 400+ peer-reviewed studies on AI-assisted clinical diagnosis, as synthesised in <em>The Lancet Digital Health</em> (2023). FDA device clearance data as of 2023.</p>
